# local-03-decode-cpu (budi, 2026-10-07): cut per-token CPU on the critical
# PP0 rank. Apply after local-02. Both parts have an off switch (env "0").
#
# py-spy of single-stream decode (fp8 slug, ~80 tok/s = 12.5 ms/token):
# Worker_PP0's main thread is never idle (PP1/PP2 wait 19-33% in recv), and
# spends ~47% building attention metadata and ~28% in the PLE host gather.
#
# 1. VLLM_MAMBA_IDX_STEP_CACHE (default 1): Flash-Next has 21 KV-cache groups,
#    so build_attn_metadata calls the GDN builder ~20x per step, and each call
#    recomputed the same "align" start indices from the same seq_lens in
#    mamba_get_block_table_tensor (~24% of PP0). build_attn_metadata now opens
#    a one-step scope; inside it the indices (and the arange) are computed once
#    per (seq_lens, block size) and only the per-group gather runs. Never
#    active during CUDA graph capture. Unit check: identical to the old path.
# 2. VLLM_PLE_GATHER_ADVISE (default 1): =0 skips only decode-06's per-step
#    process_madvise (advise_now, ~15% of PP0), keeping the prompt prefetch
#    thread (VLLM_PLE_PREFETCH). Worth it when the PLE rows are mostly resident
#    (the fp8 slug leaves ~46 GiB of page cache); misses then fault page by page.
#
# Same-boot interleaved A/B 2026-10-07 (runtime switch files, 4 rounds after
# warm-up, decode 1500 tok single stream): base 78.2, idx cache 82.3
# (+4.2 tok/s, up in all 4 rounds), advise off 76.0 (one round fell to 67.9 on
# page faults), both 80.7. Keep VLLM_PLE_GATHER_ADVISE=1. 4-stream aggregate
# was too noisy (+-13) to rank. The metadata build turned out to overlap the
# previous token's GPU work; the critical path is PP0's PLE lookup (sync of the
# sampled ids to the CPU, advise, np.take), which the cache does not touch.
